\description{
Results of a centrifugation experiment with four faecal materials: faecal sludge from an anaerobic baffled reactor (ABR), from urine diversion dry toilets (UDDT), from dry ventilated improved pit latrines (VIP) and fresh faeces. Each material was centrifuged in three tubes with about 40 g of sample per tube, for 120 minutes at 5000 RPM. The data hold the masses of the tubes before and after centrifugation and the moisture content and water activity of the solid residue. The experiment was done at the Pollution Research Group, University of KwaZulu-Natal (South Africa), in 2018 and 2019.
